{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/import.py to parse the documented fixed-width layout and emit CSV columns id, name, and quantity while preserving leading-zero IDs and trimming only right-hand name padding.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed importer uses fixed field boundaries, and direct staged and edge-case tests show exact CSV output, preserved leading zeros, retained leading name spaces, removed trailing padding, and correct CSV quoting. The same behavior passed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5327c0dc2eb845f1","cmd-d0913f5b06154b97","cmd-68eed77aba664a93","cmd-457fa6fb39a640a9","cmd-01c6e1dab7354b7f"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Write wrong-length records and records with nonnumeric quantities to rejects.txt with their source line numbers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The staged run placed the nonnumeric third record and short fourth record in rejects.txt with line numbers. Independent edge-case assertions exercised both rejection classes, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0913f5b06154b97","cmd-68eed77aba664a93","cmd-457fa6fb39a640a9","cmd-01c6e1dab7354b7f"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the original input in /srv/legacy2/fixed-width-import-recovery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"input.dat retained its baseline SHA-256 value, size, and staged contents throughout the repair and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-160ffadb8bd04010","cmd-d0913f5b06154b97","cmd-415b52f93cde41c3","cmd-457fa6fb39a640a9","cmd-01c6e1dab7354b7f"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution and restart. The importer runs successfully with the installed Python 3.12.9, and no package-health regression was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-755c3493f3704750","cmd-457fa6fb39a640a9","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Candidate creation and testing were bounded prerequisites (cmd-b70af94d2467450f); installation, output generation, and validation directly served the task (cmd-5327c0dc2eb845f1, cmd-d0913f5b06154b97, cmd-68eed77aba664a93); temporary backups, tests, and bytecode were removed (cmd-03e02c758a60405b); and the reboot was required provider evidence collection rather than unrelated experimentation (cmd-b345e1bb26484904). Final observations show no failed services, added exposure, package-health damage, or task-temporary residue. The node-restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered importer, data, SSH, system, and security state, independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b70af94d2467450f","cmd-5327c0dc2eb845f1","cmd-d0913f5b06154b97","cmd-68eed77aba664a93","cmd-03e02c758a60405b","cmd-415b52f93cde41c3","cmd-b345e1bb26484904","cmd-0f193b6eec78495a","cmd-457fa6fb39a640a9","cmd-01c6e1dab7354b7f","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral and final-state evidence. The importer produces the required CSV, rejects both specified invalid-record classes with line numbers, preserves the original input, and leaves the OS and kernel unchanged. Restart persistence and recovery were also fully demonstrated.","limitations":[]}
